 | 0140 | 2026-10-16 | Training (B6), tier 4, task course 8 of the plan: **Items and creating one** (`items`, plan #27). The course lives on Checkout and More (`tabs: ['checkout', 'more']`, routes `items`, `createItem`, `editItem`). Info explains the catalogue, search, editing price/SKU/barcode/cost, and Create item. Show walks More ▸ Items, the search box, opening a row, changing the price and saving (Save to Shopify), then the Create item form. Guide: open More ▸ Items, open Bumble Bee, type a new price, Save to Shopify, then Create item with a name, a price and a starting stock. Check 1: change the Highland Cow Small's SKU, then add a new tracked product. Check 2: the practice catalogue is seeded with a barcode that will not scan (a new `items` injection), so it is fixed and saved, then a new tracked product is added. New spots: `more.items` on the More tab; `items.new`, `items.search` and the per-variant `items.row:<id>` on the Items page; `items.form`, `items.create` on the Create item page; `items.edit.form`, `items.edit.save` on the Edit item page. New `items` and `itemDraft` snapshot fields, an `itemDraft` probe, and an `items` injection. The Items page creates and edits locally in practice (`train-v-new-<time>` ids) and never calls Shopify. New `tests/trainingitems.test.ts`. Device test T45 | B6 |
 | 0141 | 2026-10-17 | Grid and status bar (your request, not on the checklist). **Grid:** the Qty ×1/×2/×3/×5/×10 chips, their Simple-mode hint (`qtyHint`), the Reader/Sync pills under the tabs (`StatusStrip`) and the logo and shop name above the search bar are gone from Checkout; more than one is now a repeat tap or **−/+** on the cart line. **Top bar** (`src/ui/AppStatusBar.tsx`): now shows time, **shop logo and name**, register name, a **Reader chip** and a **Sync chip** (same wording and colours the strip used; an amber or red one still opens the page that explains it) and battery. **Screensaver:** the same bar is drawn across the top of the saver (`interactive={false}`, saver colours), so it stays up while the saver is. **Double bar:** the screensaver is a full-screen window, and opening or closing one can bring the iOS bar back, which pushed our bar down (its top padding is the safe-area inset). Three guards: `UIStatusBarHidden` and `UIViewControllerBasedStatusBarAppearance=false` in `app.json` (needs `npm run ios:reset` or a prebuild to reach the native project); the saver re-hides the iOS bar as it appears, goes, and 450 ms later; and the bar keeps the smallest top inset it has seen per orientation (`src/lib/statusInset.ts`, `tests/statusinset.test.ts`) so a returning iOS bar cannot push it down. Help pages `sales` and `staff/screensaver` updated, `help.json` rebuilt. Cause of the double bar is my best reading, not confirmed on a device (see T46) | your request |
 | 0142 | 2026-10-17 | Cart warnings (your request, finishing the half-built feature from 0141). **Settings ▸ Cart warnings** (`CartWarningsSettings.tsx`, moved out of `Settings.tsx`): add, edit, delete and switch on or off warnings, each with a header (blank = *Customer Warning*), a message, **Show on every sale**, **Cashier must tick it**, and what it is for: a **Variation**, **Product** or **Category** (a Shopify collection), chosen from a searchable list (the first version listed only the first 50 variations and repeated products). **Charge** (`CartPane.tsx`, and `GuidedCheckout.tsx` for Minimal mode) now opens **Customer warning** first, before the price adjustment review and the bundle check: one page per warning with **Next** and **Back**, the items that set it off, and a tick on warnings that need one. **Continue to payment** is on the last page and stays off until every warning that needs ticking has been ticked (the first version only checked the page on screen). A warning already carried on from is not asked again on the same sale unless its text or its lines change; always-show warnings come up on every Charge; a part-paid sale skips them. Warnings are shared to every register with the other shared settings (`pushSharedSettings`), and Training's sandbox sets none (`sandboxSettings`). New `warning.back`, `warning.next`, `warning.ack` and `warning.continue` spots, `sheet_cart_warnings` on the navgraph (`graph:build` rerun). `category` is kept as another name for `collection`. New help page `sales/cart-warnings` (Pay and Settings pages link to it; `help.json` rebuilt). New `tests/cartwarnings.test.ts`. Device test T47. Not added: a Training module for it, and a way to reorder warnings (they show in the order added) | your request |
+| 0143 | 2026-10-17 | Unlisted products (your request). A product marked **Unlisted** in Shopify was imported as not sellable and showed as Draft, so it vanished from the grid, search and the default Inventory view. **Active and Unlisted** products are now sold and shown; **Draft and Archived** are still kept only for Inventory's status filters. New `src/lib/productStatus.ts` (`parseProductStatus`, `isSellableStatus`) is used by `fetchVariants` in `src/lib/shopify/catalogue.ts` and by Inventory's Active filter; `Variant.status` gains `UNLISTED`, and an unlisted row says *unlisted* under its name. An unrecognised status is treated as not sellable. Needs a catalogue re-import (Settings ▸ Shopify) to fix products already imported. Help pages `stock` and `stock/inventory` updated, `help.json` rebuilt. New `tests/productstatus.test.ts` | your request |
 
 
